  "slug": "neuronal-state-4725",
  "summary": "New work pairs ex vivo single-cell tracking of glioblastoma invasion with multiome-based regulatory inference, alongside open imaging tools for live-cell phenotyping.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is quantifying single-cell state and behavior from imaging or multiome data using explicit computational models. GlioTrace combines ex vivo imaging with machine learning and probabilistic frameworks to track invasion phenotypes and state transitions in patient-derived glioblastoma. scDORI complements this at the regulatory level, inferring enhancer-driven gene regulatory networks from single-nucleus multiome data to address glioblastoma plasticity. Three preprints extend the imaging-analysis theme beyond glioblastoma: DynaCell benchmarks 3D time-lapse virtual staining, CardioShift models nested variance in cardiomyocyte Ca2+ and contractility distributions, and Organotchi automates organoid segmentation and tracking. What is new is the pairing of dynamic phenotype resolution with mechanistic or statistical structure. The items do not show that these methods transfer across systems.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
